WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.603
C++ file handling should lean on RAII.

2
00:00:02.603 --> 00:00:11.157
File stream objects, scoped handle wrappers, and custom resource owners make cleanup part of object lifetime instead of a checklist repeated in every

3
00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:11.529
branch.

4
00:00:11.529 --> 00:00:17.851
When a function returns early, throws, or rejects malformed input, owned file resources should still close predictably.

5
00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:20.454
RAII does not mean errors stop mattering.

6
00:00:20.454 --> 00:00:23.801
For input, a close failure may not affect much.

7
00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:28.636
For output, flushing or closing can be part of the operation's correctness.

8
00:00:28.636 --> 00:00:37.189
If the program must know that data reached the destination according to its durability requirements, that result needs to be checked through the

9
00:00:37.189 --> 00:00:40.164
appropriate API and reflected in the error model.

10
00:00:40.164 --> 00:00:44.255
Error handling should preserve useful state and useful information without oversharing.

11
00:00:44.255 --> 00:00:48.346
Developer diagnostics may need a category, operation name, and correlation identifier.

12
00:00:48.346 --> 00:00:50.949
User-facing messages usually need less detail.

13
00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:57.271
Sensitive paths, file contents, credentials, and internal system layout should not leak through routine errors or logs.

14
00:00:57.271 --> 00:01:00.618
Redaction should happen before data reaches broad log sinks.

15
00:01:00.618 --> 00:01:05.081
Cleanup policy should cover success, failure, parsing errors, exceptions, cancellation, and shutdown.

16
00:01:05.081 --> 00:01:12.519
Temporary files may need removal, output files may need preservation for investigation, and locks or handles may need deterministic release.

17
00:01:12.519 --> 00:01:17.725
The secure engineering goal is not simply to make the compiler accept the code.

18
00:01:17.725 --> 00:01:22.560
It is to make resource ownership and failure behavior boring, predictable, and reviewable.
